/*!
    \page sonicvia-index.html
    \title Sonic VIA

    Sonic VIA implements the QMK \l{https://www.caniusevia.com/}{VIA} HID
    keyboard protocol for RGB lighting control.

    \list
    \li \l ViaDiscovery lists VIA keyboards (HID usage page 0xff60) without
        opening them.
    \li \l ViaDevice gives blocking access to one keyboard.
    \li \l ViaProtocol sends the lighting commands, encoded for the device's
        protocol version (VIA V3, 11 and later, or legacy).
    \li \l ViaCommand builds single VIA commands.
    \endlist

    Without hidapi at build time, the library is a stub: discovery finds no
    keyboards and devices don't open.

    \section1 Using the Module

    \section2 Building with CMake

    Use the \c find_package() command to locate the SonicVia package and link
    against its target:

    \badcode
    find_package(SonicVia REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE SonicVia::SonicVia)
    \endcode

    \section1 API Reference

    \list
        \li \l{Sonic VIA C++ Classes}
    \endlist
*/
